  "published": "2026-10-24T00:57:10.72Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.3.0 (breaking): System.Text.Json is gone. [JsonModel] no longer takes a JsonSerializerContext (JsonModelContextAttribute, JsonModelImplementation, IJsonModel<TSelf>, JsonModel, JsonModelRegistry, RentedArray<T>, SerializeAsStringJsonConverter<T> and JsonElementConverter are removed; JJSON016/017 retired), JsonReadException derives from Exception (Path, LineNumber and BytePositionInLine kept), and System.Text.Json attributes are no longer read: use [JsonKey], [JsonOrder], [JsonSkip], [JsonMandatory], [JsonOptIn], [JsonOverflow] (extension data: OrderedDictionary<string, JNode?> or JObjectNode, get-only bags too) and [JsonCreator]. NonFiniteFloats defaults to AsString: NaN and ±Infinity round-trip as \"NaN\", \"Infinity\", \"-Infinity\", and JNode holds them. New ReadOnlyMembers setting ([JsonModel], [assembly: JsonDefaults], [JsonMember(ReadOnly)]) ignores computed get-only members. 10.2.0 (breaking): buffer writers are generic and passed by ref, so struct and ref struct writers work without boxing: JsonCodec.WriteJson<T, TWriter>(in T, ref TWriter) (UTF-8), JsonCodec.WriteJsonUtf16<T, TWriter>(in T, ref TWriter), JsonCodec.WriteJsonArray<T, TWriter>(..., ref TWriter), JsonTypeCodec.Write<TWriter>(object?, ref TWriter), and the generated WriteJson<TWriter>(ref TWriter); the IBufferWriter<byte|char> overloads are gone. 10.1.0: initial release. Absorbs Jakar.SystemTextJson (IJsonModel<TSelf>, [JsonModel], JsonModel, RentedArray<T>, SerializeAsStringJsonConverter<T>; still in the Jakar.Extensions namespace, diagnostics JAKAR_JSON001-007 unchanged). One attribute, [JsonModel]: without a System.Text.Json context it's Jakar.Json only; with one it implements IJsonModel<TSelf> on Jakar.Json when that supports the type (faster, fewer allocations; the context's options mirrored), otherwise on System.Text.Json (JJSON016). [GenerateJson] and JJSON010 are gone.",
